eetup.com/cinders/events/316754871/","description":"Skip the awkward first dates and come for a fun, social afternoon of pickleball & drinks with other singles 💓\n\n**Important:**\n**RSVP’ing on Meetup does not reserve your spot.**\n**To join this experience, you must sign up through [app.cinders.dating](https://app.cinders.dating/eventDetails?eventRef=j2ZrcGCWANVplf6nfDs9). Only confirmed guests will receive the exact location and details.**\n\nEvery month, we curate singles with similar hobbies, interests and profiles and invite them to join a group experience built around an activity.\n\n🥒🎾 **This month, we are doing pickleball**!\n\n**Details**\n🎾 Rotate through casual pickleball games, meet different people, hang out and have a drink between matches. Beginners welcome.\n\n🏆 A little friendly competition at the end, with a Cinders perk for the winners.\n\n📍 King East (exact meeting location will be shown to confirmed guests)\n📅 Sunday, Oct. 25 at 2pm\n👫 16 people (balanced gender)\n🎟️ Ticketed experience. Includes access to a pickleball court.\n\n**How to sign up**\n**[Sign up through cinders.dating](https://app.cinders.dating/eventDetails?eventRef=j2ZrcGCWANVplf6nfDs9). Only confirmed guests will receive the location details.**","startDate":"2026-10-25T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Cinders: Fun Activities with Curated Singles","url":"https://www.meetup.com/cinders/"},"performer":"Cinders: Fun Activities with Curated Singles"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Music Bingo with Friends! (Best of 7 Decades!)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/events/316602447/","description":"Hello everyone,\n\nI'd like to invite you out to a fun-filled afternoon with this fantastic social game called **MUSIC BINGO with Friends! (Best of 7 Decades!)**\n\nEveryone can play (It's easy to learn and most of all it's a lot of fun!)\n\n\\*Joined by my other social groups too; so we can anticipate a fabulous turn out\n\n\\*Please note we are at **The Pheasant: A Firkin Pub** at 1999 Avenue Road (roughly 6 blocks north of Lawrence - south of the 401 **(we are in the back dining area to find us)**\n\n*\\*You can also ask the wait staff or bartender if you like to show you to the group (simply ask for Steve's games event)*\n\nEvent Details Below:\n\nSincerely,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**Details of Event:**\n**Music Bingo with Friends! (Best of 7 Decades!)**\n\nMusic Bingo puts a fun musical twist on traditional bingo. Instead of listening for numbers, you'll hear familiar songs from across the decades and mark them off on your Music Bingo card.\n\nYou don't need to be a music expert — recognizing the songs, singing along and enjoying the company is all part of the fun!\n\n• **Seven decades of great music** with plenty of familiar favourites\n• **Treats for our winning participants** during the different rounds\n• **Meet and mingle** with a friendly group while enjoying a relaxed social atmosphere\n• **Come on your own or invite some friends** — we'll get everyone settled in and ready to play\n\n**Event Fee: $10**\nYour event fee includes **Music Bingo, treats for our winners, reserved seating and plenty of music, laughs and fun throughout the event.**\nPayment can be made **in cash at the event** or **in advance by e-transfer to [SteveFlemming11@gmail.com](mailto:SteveFlemming11@gmail.com)**.\nIf paying by e-transfer, please include **your name** in the message so your payment can be easily identified.\n\nBring your music memories, your sense of humour and maybe even your singing voice — although singing along is completely optional!\n\n**Friendly Reminders:**\n\nPlease arrive between **2:00 PM and 2:30 PM** so you'll have time to get settled, meet some people and get ready to play. **Music Bingo will begin shortly afterward.**\n\n\\*Great lunch menu and food specials provided:\n(One beverage or appetizer minimum upon arrival to support venue)\n\n**Parking and Transportation:**\n\\*Lots of street parking on avenue and free residential parking\n[https://www.firkinpubs.com/thepheasantandfirkin/](https://www.firkinpubs.com/thepheasantandfirkin/)\n(15-20 minute walk from Yonge & Lawrence subway station-or simply take bus or uber from the station)","startDate":"2026-10-25T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Pheasant: A Firkin Pub","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1999 Avenue Rd, North York, ON M5M 4A5, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/"},"performer":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Downtown Toronto French conversation exchange","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-toronto-french-conversation-exchange/events/316214195/","description":"This is an informal conversation group for anyone wanting to practice / use their French and meet some new people. All levels are welcome, but having a conversational level is strongly recommended (and of course native French speakers are very welcome too!). / Il s'agit d'un groupe de conversation informel pour toute personne souhaitant pratiquer / utiliser son français et rencontrer de nouvelles personnes. Tous les niveaux sont les bienvenus, mais il est recommandé d'avoir un niveau de conversation approximatif (et bien sûr, les locuteurs natifs du français sont également les bienvenus !)\n\nNous nous rencontrerons dimanche, de 14h00 à 16h00, au foodcourt de Brookfield Place, qui heureusement a beaucoup de tables et garde la musique basse!\n\n+ Juste un rappel que ce groupe est un lieu d'échange détendu avec les autres dans un esprit de respect, de tolérance et de réceptivité à la multiplicité des cultures et des niveaux de français représentés. Merci de respecter ces principes en participant aux meetups.","startDate":"2026-10-25T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Brookfield Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"181 Bay St., Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Downtown Toronto French conversation exchange","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-toronto-french-conversation-exchange/"},"performer":"Downtown Toronto French conversation exchange"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Sunday Meeple & Gaymes","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-gaymers/events/315389022/","description":"This is an opportunity to meet up for some LGBTQ2IA-flavoured gaming and socializing—allies also welcome. Come for the gaming, socializing, not to mention One Star's Hot Dog menu! :) Be sure to invite friends and such, too.\n\nAlthough Fred, your amiable host, starts the event at 3pm, feel free to drop in early as One Star opens at 2pm!\n\nYou'll have access to a robust library of board games, and attendees are welcome to bring their own games.\n\nThere is no event fee. Instead we ask attendees to purchase beverages or food from the venue since they are offering us their space for free.\n\nWe provide nametag stickers with a pronoun field; we want this to be a comfortable environment for everyone, kindly respect people's listed or stated pronouns.\n\nIf you are unsure of someone's pronouns, don't assume: Ask, Respect and Practice\nDefinitely ask before taking pictures/videos.\n\nOne Star is NOT an accessible space as the washrooms are down stairs. For those with sensory concerns, there may be possible loud noises. \\*\\*\\*Please reach out to [info@torontogaymers.ca](mailto:info@torontogaymers.ca) with any accessibility concerns.\n[https://linktr.ee/TorontoGaymers](https://linktr.ee/TorontoGaymers)\n\n#TorontoGaymers #OneStarBarTO","startDate":"2026-10-25T19:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"One Star Bar","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"538 Queen St W, Toronto, ON M5V 2B5, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Gaymers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-gaymers/"},"performer":"Toronto Gaymers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🍂🌿 NEW FALL WALK: Discover Biidaasige Park 🌿🍂","url":"https://www.meetup.com/no-such-thing-as-bad-weather/events/316183922/","description":"# 🍂🌿 **NEW FALL WALK: Discover Biidaasige Park** 🌿🍂\n\n### A Brand-New Toronto Park, Fall Colours & Waterfront Trails\n\nWe're trying something **new**!\n\nJoin us for our first group walk to **Biidaasige Park**, one of the newest and most ambitious parks in Toronto. Opened as part of the massive transformation of the Port Lands, the park sits on **Ookwemin Minising**, Toronto's new island where the Don River meets Lake Ontario.\n\nThis isn't a walk we've done before, which makes it a little more exciting. We'll spend much of the afternoon actually **exploring the park rather than rushing through it** — following its trails, enjoying the waterfront, taking in the fall scenery, and stopping along the way to appreciate the new landscape.\nThe park is enormous, with more than **50 acres already open** and more sections being added as the Port Lands transformation continues.\n\nThere are curated trails and paths, viewpoints, natural areas, and places to get down closer to the new Don River.\nAnd because we're doing this in the fall, we'll get to experience the park at a completely different time of year — cooler air, changing leaves, open skies, and fewer summer crowds. 🍂\n\nWe'll meet at the **Young Centre in the Distillery District** simply because it's an easy and convenient meeting point before we head toward the park. We won't be spending the day touring the Distillery District — **the park is the destination.**\n\n📲 **Don't Forget to join our WhatsApp Group – [\\[CLICK HERE!\\]](http://xn--[click%20here!](%20join%20our%20whatsapp%20group-cu832c:%20Click%20here%20to%20join)/)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ **What We'll Do**\n\nWe'll meet outside the **Young Centre for the Performing Arts** and make our way toward Biidaasige Park.\nOnce we reach the park, we'll slow things down and spend about **90 minutes exploring the trails and waterfront**.\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* 🍂 Enjoy the fall colours\n* 🌿 Explore the park's trails and green spaces\n* 🌊 Walk along the new waterfront landscape\n* 📸 Stop for photos and scenic views\n* 🌳 Explore the natural areas around the new Don River\n* 🌆 Take in views toward the Toronto skyline and Toronto Islands\n* 🚶‍♂️ Enjoy plenty of time to walk and talk with the group\n\nThe walk itself will be approximately **2 hours**, but we're not trying to race through it.\n**This is about experiencing the park.**\nIt's our first time doing this walk, so we'll take our time and actually enjoy discovering what has been created here.\n\n***\n\n## 🌊 **Why Biidaasige Park?**\n\nBiidaasige Park is part of one of the biggest transformations Toronto has seen in decades.\nThe new Don River was created as part of the Port Lands Flood Protection project, transforming former industrial land into a new river valley, wetlands, parkland and public spaces.\n\nThe first phase of Biidaasige Park opened in July 2025.\nThe park includes **accessible trails, cycling paths, river access, wetlands, viewpoints and waterfront promenades**, with views toward the Toronto Islands, Inner Harbour and skyline.\n\nAnd there's something particularly fun about visiting a place that is still **brand new**.\nWe're not revisiting an old Toronto favourite.\n**We're discovering somewhere new together.**\n\n***\n\n## 🍺 **After the Walk: The Keating Channel Pub & Grill**\n\nAfter exploring the park, we'll head over to **The Keating Channel Pub & Grill** for lunch.\nThe pub sits right on the Keating Channel and has been a local fixture in the area for more than 20 years. After years of Port Lands construction made the neighbourhood difficult to reach, the transformation of the area has brought new life and new visitors back to the waterfront.\nIt's a nice way to finish the day: **a brand-new park followed by one of the neighbourhood's old survivors.**\nLunch is optional, but everyone is welcome to join us.\n\n***\n\n## 🍂 **Fall Weather & Expectations**\n\nThis is a **social urban walk**, not a difficult hike.\nWe'll be walking for approximately two hours, including our time exploring the park, so you should be comfortable being on your feet for that length of time.\nPlease dress for typical Toronto fall weather. The waterfront can be cooler and windier than other parts of the city, so a warm layer is a good idea.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 **Meetup Details**\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Outside the **Young Centre for the Performing Arts**, 50 Tank House Lane, in the Distillery District. Young Centre for the Performing Arts\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time: 11:00 AM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes**.\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **End Point:** The Keating Channel Pub & Grill\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ **Meetup Fee**\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows us to continue organizing walks and events throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 **What to Bring**\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥪 A snack\n🧥 Weather-appropriate clothing\n📸 Your phone or camera for photos\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 **Who Is This For?**\n\nThis walk is great for:\n\n* People who enjoy discovering new places in Toronto\n* Anyone who likes parks and waterfront trails\n* People who want a relaxed social walk\n* Anyone interested in seeing Toronto's newest public spaces\n* People who enjoy exploring somewhere they've never been before\n* Anyone who wants to spend a fall day outside with good people\n\nThe park may be new.\n**The idea is the same: come out, walk with us, and meet some people along the way.**\n\n***\n\n📲 **You're welcome to RSVP ahead of time — or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.**\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email:\n📧 **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come discover a new park.**\n**Stay for the fall colours.**\n**Stay a little longer for lunch and friendship.** 🍂🌿🍺","startDate":"2026-10-25T15:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Young Centre for the Performing Arts","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Distillery District, 50 Tank House Lane, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"No Such Thing As Bad Weather Walking & Hiking Group!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/no-such-thing-as-bad-weather/"},"performer":"No Such Thing As Bad Weather Walking & Hiking Group!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Ghosts of West Toronto - Halloween Event 2026","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/316693116/","description":"\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearly Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours, email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or for signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket price when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nHalloween is the best time to take in the ghosts that haunt our minds and our city. The city is not quite asleep yet and things roam. They cross our paths with the stories we tell. At the core of this tour, two brutal stories that have impacted Toronto, are explored, but have a ghostly following. You could say this tour explores the old stories that stir the blood, even after 150 years.\n\nToronto is not a squeaky clean polished town, it has plenty to chill the blood. Stories of horror and crime and things that go bump in the night abound.\n\nFrom the true horror of the Mercer Reformatory to the Central Prison in Liberty Village, and the ghosts of the exhibition grounds, things that should be left alone will be dug up.\n\nMany other unexplained happenings will be talked about, this tour will haunt, or at least you hope so! Well let's get through this one alive.\n\nThis walking tour is for all levels and walkers. The tour begins at the TTC Exhibition Streetcar loop at the corner of Dufferin Street, and Springhurst Avenue in Parkdale.\n\nThis tour has a ticket price of $15.00 per person.\n\nHope to see you there. And at the end of the tour hopefully you are still around. Well maybe.....\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket price when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**","startDate":"2026-10-25T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Dufferin Gate Loop","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"on","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"160-162 Dufferin Street, Toronto, on"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto History Walks","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/"},"performer":"Toronto History Walks"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"October Recital!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-amateur-pianist-recital/events/316641076/","description":"To sign up to play, please post a comment on the meetup, reserving your spot. You attend, simply RSVP to the meetup\n\nThe time limit for each performer is 7 minutes. Please shorten your piece if it exceeds 7 minutes so everyone will have time to play\n\n======= COST ======\n\nWe use GoFundMe as a vehicle to collect donations for our costs\n\n[https://gofund.me/4ee1b73](https://gofund.me/4ee1b739)\n\nExpand the \"description\" to view an exact breakdown of costs, collected donations, and the current goal. Any additional donations above the goal will be carried forward to the next recitals\n\nGenerally, performers donate a suggested donation of $20 and attendees donate what they can\n\n======= SCHEDULE ======\n\n1 Prasa\n2 Vincent\n3 Gairus\n4 Cole\n5 Chris H\n6 Roberte\n7 Fernando\n8\n9\n10 Fabian\n11 Ken L\n12 Anthony\n13\n14\n15 Dunie\n.\nWaiting list","startDate":"2026-10-25T21:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Array Space","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"155 Walnut Avenue M6J 3W3, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Amateur Pianist Recital","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-amateur-pianist-recital/"},"performer":"Toronto Amateur Pianist Recital"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto East Weekend Gaming @ Face-to-Face Games","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-heavy-boardgamers/events/316231810/","description":"Welcome to the Sunday meetup for Toronto Heavy Boardgamers @ Face-to-Face Games!\n\nThe purpose of this event is to meet up to play heavier / longer board games, and have fun while doing it! We will start off small and if there is sufficient interest we will add capacity for future events.\n\n**Scheduling details:**\n\n\\- If you have a specific game that you would like to post for\\, feel free to do so in comments\\. In your post\\, include the name of the game\\, number of players needed for the game\\, whether you are offering a teach or not\\, and the start time \\(please try to start before noon if possible\\)\\.\n\n\\- If you would like to join a specific game that has already been posted\\, feel free to comment on it confirming your participation\\. Make sure you have noted the details posted by the host\\.\n\n\\- You are of course also welcome to organize / join games onsite on the day itself\\, assuming sufficient players / tables are available\n\n**Rules around COVID:**\n\n\\- Given this is a public event\\, we respectfully ask that only i\\) fully vaccinated individuals\\, and ii\\) those not exhibiting any COVID symptoms\\, participate\\. This requirement may change in the future based on provincial guidelines and group requirements\n\n**Admission Fee:**\n\n\\- There are no table fees for this event","startDate":"2026-10-25T15:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Face to Face Games","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1398 Danforth Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Heavy Boardgamers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-heavy-boardgamers/"},"performer":"Toronto Heavy Boardgamers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Special Event: Autumn hike through Mt. Pleasant Cemetary to Brickworks","url":"https://www.meetup.com/riverdale-5k/events/316771405/","description":"A spooky hike where we can enjoy the changing leaves in full autumn.\n\nWe will start with an inspirational walk through Mt. Pleasant Cemetary and then continuing on to the Brickworks to enjoy the remainder of the changing leaves through the Moore Ravine.\n\n**When:** Sunday, October 25, start at 1:30pm\n**Where:** Gather by the entrance on Yonge St. ([https://maps.app.goo.gl/Shqzx7fxMCBQvWJy8](https://maps.app.goo.gl/Shqzx7fxMCBQvWJy8), south of Davisville Station).\n\n**Mt. Pleasant Cemetery:** ([https://www.mountpleasantgroup.com/Locations/Cemeteries/Mount-Pleasant.aspx](https://www.mountpleasantgroup.com/Locations/Cemeteries/Mount-Pleasant.aspx \"https://www.mountpleasantgroup.com/Locations/Cemeteries/Mount-Pleasant.aspx\"))\n\n**Evergreen Brickworks:**\nhttps://www.evergreen.ca/stories/your-ultimate-fall-guide-to-evergreen-brick-works/\n\nSend me a direct message if you have any questions.","startDate":"2026-10-25T17:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Riverdale Park 5K","url":"https://www.meetup.com/riverdale-5k/"},"performer":"Riverdale Park 5K"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"The Island of Dr. Moreau","url":"https://www.meetup.com/more-than-a-classic-book-club/events/316527416/","description":"October is the month where we celebrate all things spooky, dark, and scary. Our novel this month, *The Island of Dr. Moreau*, promises to leave you disturbed - or at least, uncomfortable. It is a powerful, short, philosophical novel examining human cruelty and pain and the moral choices attached to scientific invention. Sound familiar? Written by the father of science fiction, H.G. Wells, in 1896, it explores questions such as, what happens when human intelligence challenges the very structure of nature? Highly accessible, about 115 pages, *The Island of Dr. Moreau* is a famous work that has been adapted to film, audiobooks, and other media.","startDate":"2026-10-25T19:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Demetres Desserts Distillery District","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"28 Gristmill Lane, Toronto, ON M5A 3C4, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"More Than A Classic Book Club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/more-than-a-classic-book-club/"},"performer":"More Than A Classic Book Club"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"In-Person Writing Sprints","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-science-fiction-and-fantasy-writers-meetup/events/316740744/","description":"Struggling with motivation and focus as you hammer away on your manuscript at home? Want to join a community of writers as we embrace the joys and pains (mostly pains) of writing together?\n\nBring your laptop, pen & paper, old-school typewriter, or futuristic writing gadget, and join an enthusiastic community of science fiction and fantasy writers as we work on our current projects in the same space. The format will be similar to our online writing sprints: 30-minute blocks of focused, quiet writing time (the sprints), interspersed with breaks where we can chat, ask questions, and share our writing experiences.","startDate":"2026-10-25T17:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"MaRS Discovery District","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"101 College St, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Science Fiction and Fantasy Writers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-science-fiction-and-fantasy-writers-meetup/"},"performer":"Toronto Science Fiction and Fantasy Writers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto Language Exchange | Practice Spanish & English (In-Person)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto/events/316673817/","description":"Join our **Spanish–English Language Exchange Meetup** and improve your conversation skills in a relaxed, social environment. This free event is perfect for anyone looking to practice Spanish or English while meeting new people in a cozy coffee shop setting.\n\n### **🗣️ What You’ll Do**\n\n* Practice Spanish and English through real conversations\n* Join small groups and switch languages throughout the event\n* Learn practical vocabulary and everyday expressions\n* Build confidence speaking in a supportive environment\n\n### **👥 Who Should Attend**\n\n* Spanish learners (all levels)\n* English learners (all levels)\n* Native speakers who want to help others\n* Anyone interested in language exchange and cultural connection\n\n### **☕ Venue**\n\nWe meet at a local coffee shop—just grab a drink and enjoy the conversation!\n\n### **💸 Cost**\n\n**FREE event** (please support the venue by purchasing a drink)\n\n### **🌟 Why Join?**\n\nLanguage exchanges are one of the most effective ways to learn. You’ll improve faster by speaking with real people, hearing authentic accents, and using the language in everyday situations.\nWhether you're a beginner or fluent speaker, you’ll find a welcoming community ready to practice and connect.\n\n**👉 RSVP now and start speaking with confidence!**","startDate":"2026-10-25T19:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Gatherings Restobar","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"49 St Clair Ave West,, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Language Exchange Toronto - Se Habla English & Spanish","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto/"},"performer":"Language Exchange Toronto - Se Habla English & Spanish"}]</script><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/1/0/a/6/highres_536284262.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/6/f/4/c/highres_536188492.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/d/8/0/0/highres_513475296.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/c/e/9/2/highres_534652882.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic